--TEST--
`Core\Db\Column::name` answers the label the server described — the alias wherever the select list wrote one, the table's own column name where it did not, and one entry per column rather than one per label — `rule:core-classes/db-column-types`, spec § 18
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Db\Column::name
// Run against a real engine, which is what this case needs and its siblings do
// not: a label is what the *server* described, so a claim about it that never
// prepared a statement would be a claim about this tree's own guess.
var $db = Core\Db::connect("main");
$db->execute("create table notes (id integer primary key, text text not null)", []);
$db->execute("insert into notes (id, text) values (?, ?)", [1, "buy milk"]);

// Nothing renamed: the label is the column's own name, unqualified — no table
// in front of it, which is `getColumnMeta`'s `name` and not its `table`.
foreach ($db->query("select id, text from notes", [])->columns() as Core\Db\Column $plain) {
    echo "plain ", $plain->name(), "\n";
}

// An alias wins, and it wins for an expression too — an expression with no
// alias is labelled by the server and that label is not pinned here, which is
// why every column below writes one.
foreach ($db->query("select id as reference, text as body from notes", [])->columns()
    as Core\Db\Column $renamed) {
    echo "renamed ", $renamed->name(), "\n";
}

// One entry per *column* and not per label, which is the bound that makes this
// an array and never a map: two columns may carry one label, and a map would
// have lost the second.
var $twice = $db->query("select id, id from notes", [])->columns();
echo "twice ", Core\Arr::count($twice), " ", $twice[0]->name(), " ", $twice[1]->name(), "\n";

// And the description belongs to the statement rather than to a row, so a
// `select` that matched nothing still has its labels.
var $none = $db->query("select id as reference from notes where id < 0", []);
echo "empty ", $none->count(), " ", $none->columns()[0]->name(), "\n";
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.db]
connect = ["main"]

[db.main]
driver = "sqlite"
path = ":memory:"
--EXPECT--
plain id
plain text
renamed reference
renamed body
twice 2 id id
empty 0 reference
